<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/leaflet/1.9.4/leaflet.min.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/maplibre-gl/4.7.1/maplibre-gl.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/boring-cities/style.css' | relative_url }}">
<div class="bc in-blog tex2jax_ignore mathjax_ignore">
<div class="pills" id="city-pills" role="group" aria-label="Choose a city"></div>
<div class="headline" id="headline" aria-live="polite"></div>
<p class="note" id="seedline"></p>
<div id="stackbar" class="stackbar" role="img"></div>
<div class="legend" id="legend"></div>
<label class="strict"><input type="checkbox" id="strict"> <span id="strict-label"></span></label>

<section id="s-compare" hidden>
<h2>How the cities compare</h2>
<div class="pills" id="cmp-pills" role="group" aria-label="Cities to compare"></div>
<p class="note" id="compare-note"></p>
<div id="heat"></div>
<h3>What one city has that another doesn't</h3>
<div class="filters" id="diff-controls"></div>
<div id="diff" class="diff"></div>
<h3>Everyday profile</h3>
<div class="table-wrap"><table id="profile"></table></div>
<h3>Venues on the map (OpenStreetMap, within 25&nbsp;km of the centre; bar length is the square root of the count)</h3>
<p class="note">Raw counts depend on how thoroughly each city has been mapped, so read them as a rough order of magnitude.</p>
<div id="density"></div>
</section>

<section id="s-categories">
<h2>Where <span class="cn">this city</span> is rich (and thin)</h2>
<p class="note">Share of each category's activities that can be done here. Click a bar to filter everything below.</p>
<div id="cat-chart"></div>
</section>

<section id="s-treemap">
<h2>Every activity, one box each</h2>
<p class="note">One square per activity, grouped by category: blue = doable here, orange = partly (limited or simulated), faint grey = not possible. Hover a square for the venue and click it to jump to its row; click a heading to filter everything else to that category.</p>
<div id="treemap"></div>
</section>

<section id="s-map">
<h2>Where it happens</h2>
<p class="note">Blue dots are researched venues for specific activities. Gray points are sports, park, arts, craft and learning venues in OpenStreetMap &mdash; the background hum of the city. Rings are 5 km and 15 km from <span id="centre-name">the centre</span>.</p>
<div class="map-controls" id="map-controls"></div>
<div id="map"></div>
</section>

<section id="s-grid">
<h2>What it costs, how far it is</h2>
<p class="note">Each dot is one doable activity. Hover a dot; click a cell to filter the table.</p>
<div id="grid"></div>
</section>

<section id="s-no">
<h2>What you genuinely can't do here</h2>
<p class="note">Honest accounting: these need terrain, climate, animals or a law that doesn't exist in the metro area.</p>
<div id="nolist" class="nolist"></div>
</section>

<section id="s-table">
<h2>The full list</h2>
<div class="filters" id="filters"></div>
<div class="table-wrap"><table id="table"></table></div>
<p class="note" id="table-count"></p>
</section>

<footer>
<h2>How this was made</h2>
<p id="method"></p>
<p><a href="{{ '/assets/boring-cities/activities.csv' | relative_url }}" download>Download the data (CSV, all cities)</a> &middot; <a href="{{ '/assets/boring-cities/data.json' | relative_url }}" download>JSON</a></p>
</footer>
<div id="tip" class="tip" hidden></div>
</div>
